    "For U1, implement queue/topic cleanup via a new plugin that handles module undeployments, checking for last consumer and removing queue/binding/exchange. The stream destroy command will have an optional `--clean` flag to trigger this cleanup.",
    "For U2, use Spring Integration's error channel pattern: each module will have an error channel, and exceptions will be published to a stream-specific error channel that users can tap into.",
    "For U3, secure all REST endpoints using Spring Security with Spring Boot auto-configuration. Support basic authentication for DSL shell and form-based login for Admin UI. Configuration via application.yml.",
    "For U4, document all available SpEL keys in the reference guide.",
    "For U5, create a new HTTP source module that embeds Tomcat and uses Spring MVC's DispatcherServlet, providing full header mapping and content-type negotiation.",
    "For U6, implement both client-side polling (for shell) and server-sent events (SSE) for Admin UI to receive real-time deployment status updates.",
    "For U7, implement SFTP source module using Spring Integration's SftpInboundFileSynchronizer and SftpInboundFileSynchronizingMessageSource, with configuration options for connection and file filtering.",
    "For U8, implement ElasticSearch sink module using Spring Data Elasticsearch, supporting bulk indexing and configurable index/type mapping."
  ],
